OL,3,ABBC upholds complaints over Victoria
OL,4,ABeckham slur on Have I Got News For You
OL,5,
OL,6,FComplaints about the broadcast of a
OL,7,Fswear word in connection with Victoria
OL,8,FBeckham during an episode of BBC One's
OL,9,FHave I Got News For You have been
OL,10,Fupheld, the corporation's executive
OL,11,Fcomplaints unit (ECU) has ruled.
OL,13,FThe show, from 7 November last year,
OL,14,Fhosted by comic and presenter Katherine
OL,15,FRyan, featured an email allegedly sent
OL,16,Fby Sir David Beckham in which the word
OL,17,Fwas used.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790293689
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ABBC upholds complaints over Victoria
OL,4,ABeckham slur on Have I Got News For You
OL,5,
OL,6,FRyan told the show's panellists: "I
OL,7,Fdon't know that we are allowed to
OL,8,Fbroadcast the c-word, but you did
OL,9,Freference Victoria Beckham earlier and
OL,10,Fwe'll allow that."
OL,12,FTwo viewers complained that this was
OL,13,Fgratuitously offensive, and the BBC
OL,14,Fsaid there was no justification for a
OL,15,Fcomment which "presented Victoria
OL,16,FBeckham as equivalent to a particularly
OL,17,Foffensive word".
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
